<question type="stack">
  <name><text>PDE BVP - Q5: u_x=0, uniqueness and solution</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The PDE \(\dfrac{\partial u}{\partial x} = 0\) has infinitely many solutions without an extra condition.</p>
<p>Given the condition \(u(0,y) = {@ic@}\), find the unique solution.</p>
<p>\(u(x,y) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text></questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<h3>Solution</h3>
<p>Integrating \(u_x=0\) w.r.t. \(x\) gives \(u(x,y) = f(y)\), an arbitrary function of \(y\).</p>
<p>Applying \(u(0,y) = {@ic@}\): \(f(y) = {@ic@}\).</p>
<p>Therefore \(u(x,y) = {@ta1@}\).</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
